# Home Lab Telegram bot — units the /restart executor may target.
#
# Installed to /etc/homelab-telegram-bot/restart-allowlist
#
# THIS IS THE SECOND GATE, NOT THE ONLY ONE.
#
# The first is the polkit rule in /etc/polkit-1/rules.d/50-homelab-bot.rules,
# which is evaluated inside PID 1 and is scoped to one user, one unit and one
# verb. This file is checked inside the bot before it even calls systemctl.
#
# Neither trusts the other. A bug in the bot cannot reach a unit polkit refuses;
# a mistake in the polkit rule cannot reach a unit this file does not name.
# Adding a line here does NOT grant anything on its own.
#
# NEVER add a unit whose loss would cost access to this machine. From
# docs/standards/safe-changes-headless.md, that means at minimum:
#
#   ssh, tailscaled, systemd-networkd, systemd-resolved, wpa_supplicant,
#   netplan-wpa-*, systemd-logind, dbus, polkit
#
# The node has no console. A service you cannot restart is an inconvenience; a
# network you cannot reach is a trip to find a monitor.

chrony.service
